    {
      "game": "Assetto Corsa Competizione",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/3153/450x258/assetto-corsa-competizione-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1786698000",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/3153-buy-assetto-corsa-competizione-pc-steam/",
      "user": "gamer-4c440b8",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Game is super cheap. It is the best to start as a sim-racing or to try your skills. Then you can start to buy the DLC, before of that, you have a lot of online races to play. Community is active and there are a lot of races everyday, everytime."
    },
    {
      "game": "Yakuza: Like a Dragon Legendary Hero Edition",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/7514/450x258/yakuza-like-a-dragon-legendary-hero-edition-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1786698000",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/7514-buy-yakuza-like-a-dragon-legendary-hero-edition-pc-steam/",
      "user": "Kreton [Loli-Hunter Gaming]",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/26599485-1769446019.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Another Yakuza installment that turns both the world and the gameplay completely upside down. As usual, a serious story about the Japanese yakuza is turned into a comedy, this time starring a gangster with a serious case of chuunibyou.\n\nNice graphics, great music, a huge variety of activities, interesting characters, tons of humor, and all of it wrapped in a JRPG coating. The biggest downside is probably the amount of grinding, because experience points come in painfully slowly.\n\n9/10, highly recommended."
    }
